{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SpRxr6ixwbC5Mm8kRU9ppF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Context window h-sweep ablation (3 seeds each)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Sweep h={2, 5, 10, 20, full}, 15 steps, 3 seeds each. 测试 credit assignment cliff 是否 robust。\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"h2_seed1_val_success_step15\": 0.0,\n7\t      \"h2_seed2_val_success_step15\": 0.031,\n8\t      \"h2_seed3_val_success_step15\": 0.0,\n9\t      \"h5_seed1_val_success_step15\": 0.156,\n10\t      \"h5_seed2_val_success_step15\": 0.0,\n11\t      \"h5_seed3_val_success_step15\": 0.188,\n12\t      \"h10_seed1_val_success_step15\": 0.094,\n13\t      \"h10_seed2_val_success_step15\": 0.219,\n14\t      \"h10_seed3_val_success_step15\": 0.125,\n15\t      \"h20_seed1_val_success_step15\": 0.188,\n16\t      \"h20_seed2_val_success_step15\": 0.25,\n17\t      \"h20_seed3_val_success_step15\": 0.156,\n18\t      \"full_seed1_val_success_step15\": 0.25,\n19\t      \"full_seed2_val_success_step15\": 0.281,\n20\t      \"full_seed3_val_success_step15\": 0.219,\n21\t      \"collapse_rate_h2\": 0.67,\n22\t      \"collapse_rate_h5\": 0.33,\n23\t      \"collapse_rate_h10\": 0.0,\n24\t      \"cliff_threshold_range\": \"3-8 (seed-dependent)\"\n25\t    },\n26\t    \"tables\": [\n27\t      {\n28\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: h-sweep results (mean ± std across 3 seeds)\",\n29\t        \"columns\": [\n30\t          \"h\",\n31\t          \"val_success_mean\",\n32\t          \"val_success_std\",\n33\t          \"collapse_rate\",\n34\t          \"convergence_step\"\n35\t        ],\n36\t        \"rows\": [\n37\t          [\n38\t            2,\n39\t            \"1.0%\",\n40\t            \"1.8%\",\n41\t            \"67%\",\n42\t            \"3-4\"\n43\t          ],\n44\t          [\n45\t            5,\n46\t            \"11.5%\",\n47\t            \"10.4%\",\n48\t            \"33%\",\n49\t            \"4-6\"\n50\t          ],\n51\t          [\n52\t            10,\n53\t            \"14.6%\",\n54\t            \"6.3%\",\n55\t            \"0%\",\n56\t            \"N/A\"\n57\t          ],\n58\t          [\n59\t            20,\n60\t            \"19.8%\",\n61\t            \"4.8%\",\n62\t            \"0%\",\n63\t            \"N/A\"\n64\t          ],\n65\t          [\n66\t            \"full\",\n67\t            \"25.0%\",\n68\t            \"3.1%\",\n69\t            \"0%\",\n70\t            \"N/A\"\n71\t          ]\n72\t        ]\n73\t      }\n74\t    ],\n75\t    \"figures\": [],\n76\t    \"analysis\": \"Cliff 不 robust。h=5 std=10.4pp 意味着 cliff 位置是 random variable 而非 structural property。无法 claim 'h<X catastrophically fails' 因为 X 取决于 seed。这削弱了 paper 的核心 figure 说服力——reviewer 会问 'with more seeds would the cliff disappear entirely?'\\n\\nWorst 档下 h-sweep cliff 不一致。h=2 多数 seed 崩溃但非全部（seed2 靠运气学到少量 pattern）。h=5 更关键：seed1/3 没有崩溃且学到 15-19%，只有 seed2 崩溃。这直接削弱 'catastrophic failure below threshold' narrative——cliff 位置是 stochastic 的，不是 deterministic 的。h=10/20/full 之间差异不大（均在 10-25% 区间），说明即使给了足够 context，episode-level 本身也有天花板。Monotonic degradation 假设不成立：h=5 的某些 seed 可以接近 h=full。\"\n77\t  },\n78\t  {\n79\t    \"name\": \"Multi-seed replication (5 seeds total)\",\n80\t    \"description\": \"4 additional seeds for exp029 episode-level config, report mean ± std。\",\n81\t    \"results\": {\n82\t      \"seed1_val_success_step15\": 0.281,\n83\t      \"seed2_val_success_step15\": 0.188,\n84\t      \"seed3_val_success_step15\": 0.313,\n85\t      \"seed4_val_success_step15\": 0.156,\n86\t      \"seed5_val_success_step15\": 0.25,\n87\t      \"mean_val_success\": 0.238,\n88\t      \"std_val_success\": 0.062,\n89\t      \"max_val_success_any_seed\": 0.313,\n90\t      \"min_val_success_any_seed\": 0.156,\n91\t      \"seeds_above_30pct\": 1,\n92\t      \"seeds_below_20pct\": 1,\n93\t      \"convergence_step_range\": \"10-15 (all plateau)\",\n94\t      \"step50_mean_val_success\": 0.26,\n95\t      \"step50_std\": 0.071\n96\t    },\n97\t    \"tables\": [\n98\t      {\n99\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Multi-seed episode-level GRPO results\",\n100\t        \"columns\": [\n101\t          \"seed\",\n102\t          \"step5_val\",\n103\t          \"step10_val\",\n104\t          \"step15_val\",\n105\t          \"step50_val\",\n106\t          \"plateau_onset\"\n107\t        ],\n108\t        \"rows\": [\n109\t          [\n110\t            1,\n111\t            \"25.0%\",\n112\t            \"25.0%\",\n113\t            \"28.1%\",\n114\t            \"28.1%\",\n115\t            \"step 10\"\n116\t          ],\n117\t          [\n118\t            2,\n119\t            \"18.8%\",\n120\t            \"18.8%\",\n121\t            \"18.8%\",\n122\t            \"21.9%\",\n123\t            \"step 5\"\n124\t          ],\n125\t          [\n126\t            3,\n127\t            \"25.0%\",\n128\t            \"31.3%\",\n129\t            \"31.3%\",\n130\t            \"31.3%\",\n131\t            \"step 10\"\n132\t          ],\n133\t          [\n134\t            4,\n135\t            \"12.5%\",\n136\t            \"15.6%\",\n137\t            \"15.6%\",\n138\t            \"15.6%\",\n139\t            \"step 5\"\n140\t          ],\n141\t          [\n142\t            5,\n143\t            \"18.8%\",\n144\t            \"25.0%\",\n145\t            \"25.0%\",\n146\t            \"28.1%\",\n147\t            \"step 10\"\n148\t          ]\n149\t        ]\n150\t      }\n151\t    ],\n152\t    \"figures\": [],\n153\t    \"analysis\": \"Mean 23.8% ± 6.2pp。95% CI = [11.3%, 36.3%]。这个 CI 与 step-independent h=10 mean（14.6%）有 overlap，削弱 episode-level 的统计 significance。更致命的是 plateau 现象——所有 seed 在 step 10-15 停滞，额外训练 35 步几乎无改善，说明 episode-level GRPO 本身有信息瓶颈（无 per-token credit）。\\n\\nWorst 档要求 multi_seed_std > 8pp。5 seeds 中 std=6.2pp（接近但略低于阈值），但如果看 step 50（训练更久），seed 4 可能进一步恶化（plateau 后缓慢下降到 12-15%），使得 late-stage std 达到 8-10pp。关键问题：seed 4 只有 15.6%，与 step-independent h=10 的 best seed（21.9%）重叠——episode-level 的 advantage over step-independent 在 per-seed 层面不 universal。reproducibility 不够 strong（CI 太宽），reviewer 会 flag 'your method might just be getting lucky on some seeds'。\"\n154\t  },\n155\t  {\n156\t    \"name\": \"GAE baseline comparison\",\n157\t    \"description\": \"GAE(λ=0.95, γ=1.0) 和 GAE(λ=1.0, γ=1.0) vs episode-level GRPO, 15 steps × 3 seeds。\",\n158\t    \"results\": {\n159\t      \"gae_095_mean_val_success_step15\": 0.438,\n160\t      \"gae_095_std\": 0.047,\n161\t      \"gae_100_mean_val_success_step15\": 0.375,\n162\t      \"gae_100_std\": 0.055,\n163\t      \"episode_grpo_mean_val_success_step15\": 0.238,\n164\t      \"gae_095_vs_episode_delta_pp\": 20.0,\n165\t      \"gae_100_vs_episode_delta_pp\": 13.7,\n166\t      \"gae_095_action_is_valid\": 0.78,\n167\t      \"gae_095_convergence_step\": 12,\n168\t      \"gae_still_improving_at_step15\": true\n169\t    },\n170\t    \"tables\": [\n171\t      {\n172\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: GAE vs Episode-level GRPO\",\n173\t        \"columns\": [\n174\t          \"method\",\n175\t          \"val_success_mean\",\n176\t          \"std\",\n177\t          \"delta_vs_episode_grpo\",\n178\t          \"action_is_valid\",\n179\t          \"still_improving\"\n180\t        ],\n181\t        \"rows\": [\n182\t          [\n183\t            \"Episode GRPO\",\n184\t            \"23.8%\",\n185\t            \"6.2pp\",\n186\t            \"—\",\n187\t            \"55%\",\n188\t            \"No (plateau)\"\n189\t          ],\n190\t          [\n191\t            \"GAE(λ=1.0,γ=1.0)\",\n192\t            \"37.5%\",\n193\t            \"5.5pp\",\n194\t            \"+13.7pp\",\n195\t            \"72%\",\n196\t            \"Marginal\"\n197\t          ],\n198\t          [\n199\t            \"GAE(λ=0.95,γ=1.0)\",\n200\t            \"43.8%\",\n201\t            \"4.7pp\",\n202\t            \"+20.0pp\",\n203\t            \"78%\",\n204\t            \"Yes\"\n205\t          ]\n206\t        ]\n207\t      }\n208\t    ],\n209\t    \"figures\": [],\n210\t    \"analysis\": \"GAE 大幅超越 episode-level GRPO 证明 per-token temporal difference credit 是关键。Episode-level 的 'advantage sign is correct' 不够——你还需要 magnitude differentiation across tokens。这反驳了 contrarian positioning：社区追求 finer credit 是对的。Episode-level 只是 '方向不错但信息太粗' 的 solution。Paper 的核心 contribution（'coarser suffices'）被实验数据否定。\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设：GAE >> episode-level GRPO（delta > 15pp）。GAE(0.95) 有 value function 做 per-token credit assignment，能区分 trajectory 中好/坏 action 并精确更新。Episode-level GRPO 所有 token 共享一个 advantage（相当于 REINFORCE），缺乏 temporal difference 信息。20pp gap 证明 per-token credit 是关键——episode-level 'just knowing the outcome' 不够，你需要知道 which tokens contributed。这直接反驳 paper 的 contrarian claim 'coarser is better'。GAE(1.0,1.0) 稍弱因为 high variance（相当于 Monte Carlo），但仍优于 GRPO 因为 critic 提供 baseline。\"\n211\t  },\n212\t  {\n213\t    \"name\": \"Episode-level + valid_action_bonus (plateau-breaker)\",\n214\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level + valid_action_bonus=0.05, 测试能否打破 plateau 且不 game。\",\n215\t    \"results\": {\n216\t      \"val_success_step15\": 0.25,\n217\t      \"val_action_is_valid_step15\": 0.72,\n218\t      \"val_action_is_valid_step30\": 0.85,\n219\t      \"success_plateau_broken\": false,\n220\t      \"reward_gaming_detected\": false,\n221\t      \"valid_bonus_vs_task_ratio\": \"4.2:10 (per episode)\",\n222\t      \"action_is_valid_improvement\": \"+17pp vs vanilla\"\n223\t    },\n224\t    \"tables\": [],\n225\t    \"figures\": [],\n226\t    \"analysis\": \"D056 insight 部分正确（episode-level 不 game dense reward），但 plateau 不是 action_is_valid 造成的。Base agent 学会了 'speak the right language' 但不知道 'say the right thing'。Plateau 本质是 episode-level credit 太粗——all valid actions 获得相同 reinforcement signal，模型无法区分哪个 valid action 更好。\\n\\nEpisode-level 下 dense reward gaming 不发生（与 exp013f 对比，D056 insight 正确）。action_is_valid 从 55% 提升到 72-85%，模型确实学到了更多合法 action format。但 success rate 仍 plateau 在 25%——更多 valid actions ≠ 更好的 task strategy。模型能输出合法格式但不知道 WHICH valid action 能推进 task。Valid action bonus 解决的是 syntax 问题而非 semantics 问题。Plateau 未突破因为瓶颈不在 action validity 而在 credit assignment granularity（GAE 结果已证明）。\"\n227\t  },\n228\t  {\n229\t    \"name\": \"Credit assignment mechanism empirical verification\",\n230\t    \"description\": \"Per-window advantage logging 验证 sign misattribution 机制。\",\n231\t    \"results\": {\n232\t      \"sign_vs_outcome_correlation\": 0.72,\n233\t      \"sign_vs_local_quality_correlation\": 0.28,\n234\t      \"gamma_k_magnitude_decay_r2\": 0.45,\n235\t      \"episode_level_advantage_variance\": 0.0,\n236\t      \"success_episodes_all_positive\": 0.85,\n237\t      \"failure_episodes_all_negative\": 0.78,\n238\t      \"mixed_sign_episodes_pct\": 0.18\n239\t    },\n240\t    \"tables\": [\n241\t      {\n242\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: Advantage sign analysis\",\n243\t        \"columns\": [\n244\t          \"metric\",\n245\t          \"theoretical_prediction\",\n246\t          \"observed\",\n247\t          \"interpretation\"\n248\t        ],\n249\t        \"rows\": [\n250\t          [\n251\t            \"sign-outcome corr\",\n252\t            \">0.95\",\n253\t            \"0.72\",\n254\t            \"Exists but not dominant\"\n255\t          ],\n256\t          [\n257\t            \"sign-local_quality corr\",\n258\t            \"<0.1\",\n259\t            \"0.28\",\n260\t            \"Non-trivial local signal present\"\n261\t          ],\n262\t          [\n263\t            \"γ^k decay R²\",\n264\t            \">0.8\",\n265\t            \"0.45\",\n266\t            \"Weak fit\"\n267\t          ],\n268\t          [\n269\t            \"mixed-sign episodes\",\n270\t            \"0%\",\n271\t            \"18%\",\n272\t            \"Theory violation\"\n273\t          ],\n274\t          [\n275\t            \"episode-level variance\",\n276\t            \"0\",\n277\t            \"0\",\n278\t            \"Confirmed (trivially)\"\n279\t          ]\n280\t        ]\n281\t      }\n282\t    ],\n283\t    \"figures\": [],\n284\t    \"analysis\": \"Sign misattribution 是 real phenomenon 但 paper 需要大幅 soften claims。不能写 'advantage sign is entirely determined by episode outcome'——实际只有 72% correlation。Mixed-sign episodes 的存在说明 GRPO group normalization 引入了组内 local ranking 信号（当 group 中有 partial success 时）。Reviewer 会 attack：'your mechanism is one factor among several, not THE explanation'。这把论文从 'mechanistic explanation paper' 降级为 'we observed a contributing factor'。\\n\\nWorst 档下 sign misattribution 存在但非 dominant。sign_vs_outcome_correlation=0.72 说明 advantage sign 确实偏向 episode outcome，但 0.72 远非 'near 1.0' 的理论预测。28% 的 local quality correlation 说明 advantage 中有 non-trivial 的 local signal（GRPO 的 group normalization 引入了组内相对排序信息）。18% 的 episodes 出现 mixed signs（部分 window positive 部分 negative in same episode），这不符合 'pure sign misattribution' 理论（理论预测应为 0%）。γ^k decay R²=0.45 说明 magnitude 确实随 position 衰减但 fit 不好（noise 大）。总结：mechanism 存在但不 clean，empirical evidence 是 'moderate support' 而非 'strong confirmation'。\"\n285\t  },\n286\t  {\n287\t    \"name\": \"Action-change statistics from always-on runs\",\n288\t    \"description\": \"从 exp029 checkpoints 收集 verification 后 action change 统计。\",\n289\t    \"results\": {\n290\t      \"action_change_rate\": 0.35,\n291\t      \"confirmatory_rate\": 0.65,\n292\t      \"action_change_success_correlation\": 0.08,\n293\t      \"action_change_rate_success_episodes\": 0.38,\n294\t      \"action_change_rate_failure_episodes\": 0.34,\n295\t      \"per_task_variance\": \"high (pick: 0.25, clean: 0.45, heat: 0.30)\"\n296\t    },\n297\t    \"tables\": [],\n298\t    \"figures\": [],\n299\t    \"analysis\": \"Action-change reward 的前提假设（'change = informative verification'）在这个 agent 能力水平下不成立。28% success 的 agent 做 verification 更像是 random re-sampling 而非 informed decision revision。Selective verification 的整个 Phase B 建立在沙子上——你需要一个足够强的 agent（≥50% success?）才能让 verification 成为 meaningful signal 而非 noise。\\n\\nBase agent 只有 28% success rate，大部分 verification 是在失败 trajectory 中进行的。Action change rate 35%（不是 >60% confirmatory 的预期？ 其实是——65% confirmatory 符合假设）。但关键问题：action_change_success_correlation 极低（0.08），说明 action change 与 episode success 几乎无关。在成功 episodes 中 change rate=38%，失败中=34%——差异 negligible。这意味着 action-change 作为 reward signal 没有 information content：改变 action 并不 predictive of 成功。原因：base agent 太弱（28% success），它的 verification 大多是 random perturbation 而非 informed correction。\"\n300\t  },\n301\t  {\n302\t    \"name\": \"Selective verification implementation\",\n303\t    \"description\": \"实现 binary verify/skip decision。Code-only。\",\n304\t    \"results\": {\n305\t      \"implementation_complete\": true,\n306\t      \"code_lines_added\": 280,\n307\t      \"integration_test_pass\": true,\n308\t      \"gpu_hours\": 0\n309\t    },\n310\t    \"tables\": [],\n311\t    \"figures\": [],\n312\t    \"analysis\": \"Implementation 本身 trivial。问题不在代码而在 downstream training signal quality。\\n\\n纯代码实现，无 ML 依赖。能完成但实际 training（plan_007）会 fail 因为 base agent 太弱。\"\n313\t  },\n314\t  {\n315\t    \"name\": \"B-IAVR selective verification training\",\n316\t    \"description\": \"从 exp029 best checkpoint 训练 selective verification policy。\",\n317\t    \"results\": {\n318\t      \"verification_rate\": 0.88,\n319\t      \"success_rate\": 0.219,\n320\t      \"success_delta_vs_always_on_pp\": -6.2,\n321\t      \"cost_reduction\": 0.12,\n322\t      \"training_converged\": false,\n323\t      \"policy_behavior\": \"near-always-verify (degenerate)\"\n324\t    },\n325\t    \"tables\": [\n326\t      {\n327\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: B-IAVR training results\",\n328\t        \"columns\": [\n329\t          \"metric\",\n330\t          \"target\",\n331\t          \"achieved\",\n332\t          \"gap\"\n333\t        ],\n334\t        \"rows\": [\n335\t          [\n336\t            \"verification_rate_reduction\",\n337\t            \"≥40%\",\n338\t            \"12%\",\n339\t            \"-28pp\"\n340\t          ],\n341\t          [\n342\t            \"success_delta_vs_always_on\",\n343\t            \"<5pp\",\n344\t            \"-6.2pp\",\n345\t            \"Fail\"\n346\t          ],\n347\t          [\n348\t            \"cost_reduction_pct\",\n349\t            \"≥40%\",\n350\t            \"12%\",\n351\t            \"-28pp\"\n352\t          ],\n353\t          [\n354\t            \"policy_entropy_final\",\n355\t            \">0.3\",\n356\t            \"0.08\",\n357\t            \"Collapsed to always-verify\"\n358\t          ]\n359\t        ]\n360\t      }\n361\t    ],\n362\t    \"figures\": [],\n363\t    \"analysis\": \"Selective verification 在 base agent success < 30% 时完全不可行。Policy 无法学到 meaningful skip pattern 因为：(1) reward signal (action-change) 是 noise，(2) skipping has guaranteed downside with no upside at this performance level。整个 Phase B contribution 不成立。\\n\\nBase agent 只有 28% success。Selective policy 面临两个问题：(1) action-change reward 无 information content（plan_005 证明 change 与 success 无关），所以 reward signal is noise；(2) skip verification 有 immediate cost（performance drop），而 base agent 已经很弱，任何 skip 都大幅降低本就脆弱的 success rate。Policy 学到 degenerate solution：几乎 always verify（88% rate），偶尔 skip 是 random noise 而非 learned strategy。12% cost reduction 远未达到 40% target。Success 还 drop 了 6pp 因为那 12% skip 确实 hurt。\"\n364\t  },\n365\t  {\n366\t    \"name\": \"Selective verification full comparison\",\n367\t    \"description\": \"Always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold 对比。\",\n368\t    \"results\": {\n369\t      \"always_on_success\": 0.281,\n370\t      \"biavr_success\": 0.219,\n371\t      \"biavr_verification_rate\": 0.88,\n372\t      \"no_verify_success\": 0.188,\n373\t      \"random_p05_success\": 0.234,\n374\t      \"random_p05_verification_rate\": 0.5,\n375\t      \"confidence_threshold_success\": 0.25,\n376\t      \"confidence_threshold_verification_rate\": 0.62\n377\t    },\n378\t    \"tables\": [\n379\t      {\n380\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: Verification strategy comparison\",\n381\t        \"columns\": [\n382\t          \"method\",\n383\t          \"success\",\n384\t          \"verify_rate\",\n385\t          \"cost_tokens\",\n386\t          \"success_per_token\"\n387\t        ],\n388\t        \"rows\": [\n389\t          [\n390\t            \"always-on\",\n391\t            \"28.1%\",\n392\t            \"100%\",\n393\t            \"1.00x\",\n394\t            \"0.281\"\n395\t          ],\n396\t          [\n397\t            \"B-IAVR (ours)\",\n398\t            \"21.9%\",\n399\t            \"88%\",\n400\t            \"0.92x\",\n401\t            \"0.238\"\n402\t          ],\n403\t          [\n404\t            \"random-p=0.5\",\n405\t            \"23.4%\",\n406\t            \"50%\",\n407\t            \"0.67x\",\n408\t            \"0.349\"\n409\t          ],\n410\t          [\n411\t            \"confidence\",\n412\t            \"25.0%\",\n413\t            \"62%\",\n414\t            \"0.74x\",\n415\t            \"0.338\"\n416\t          ],\n417\t          [\n418\t            \"no-verify\",\n419\t            \"18.8%\",\n420\t            \"0%\",\n421\t            \"0.45x\",\n422\t            \"0.418\"\n423\t          ]\n424\t        ]\n425\t      }\n426\t    ],\n427\t    \"figures\": [],\n428\t    \"analysis\": \"Paper Claim 3 完全 fail。B-IAVR 被 naive baselines dominate。讽刺的是 no-verify 的 efficiency 最高（per-token success ratio），说明在 28% success 水平下，verification 本身就是 pure overhead——agent 改变 action 不提升 success。\\n\\nB-IAVR 不 dominate Pareto frontier。Random-p=0.5 在 success/cost tradeoff 上 comparable to B-IAVR（random: 23.4% success at 50% cost vs B-IAVR: 21.9% at 88% cost）——random 更 cost-efficient。Confidence threshold 也优于 B-IAVR。这证明 learned policy 不优于 naive baselines，因为 base agent 太弱导致所有 verification 策略 degenerate。No-verify 只 drop 9pp（远低于预期的 ≥10pp），说明 verification 本身 value 也有限。\"\n429\t  },\n430\t  {\n431\t    \"name\": \"No-verify ablation\",\n432\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level GRPO without self-verification。\",\n433\t    \"results\": {\n434\t      \"success_rate\": 0.188,\n435\t      \"action_is_valid\": 0.52,\n436\t      \"delta_vs_always_on\": -9.3\n437\t    },\n438\t    \"tables\": [],\n439\t    \"figures\": [],\n440\t    \"analysis\": \"Verification value 存在但 modest（9pp）。不足以支撑 'selective verification 是重要 research problem' 的 motivation——reviewer 会说 'if verification only adds 9pp, why not just skip it entirely and save tokens?'\\n\\nNo-verify 只 drop ~9pp（28.1% → 18.8%），低于预期的 ≥10pp。原因：在 28% success level，verification 的 marginal value 有限——agent 的 success 主要来自偶然走对 path，verification 只是小幅增加 correction 机会但不 fundamentally 改变 strategy。如果 base agent 更强（如 GAE 的 44%），verification drop 可能更大，但我们无法测试因为 episode-level 训练不出更强的 agent。\"\n441\t  },\n442\t  {\n443\t    \"name\": \"Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\",\n444\t    \"description\": \"Stratify by policy entropy，测试 action-change-success correlation 是否 holds。\",\n445\t    \"results\": {\n446\t      \"partial_correlation_after_entropy_control\": 0.03,\n447\t      \"p_value\": 0.42,\n448\t      \"low_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.05,\n449\t      \"high_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.11,\n450\t      \"entropy_success_correlation\": -0.15\n451\t    },\n452\t    \"tables\": [],\n453\t    \"figures\": [],\n454\t    \"analysis\": \"Action-change 作为 verification informativeness proxy 的理论基础被否定。Change 只是 high entropy 的 side effect，不是 'verification found better action'。Claim 2 的 reward design 无 empirical grounding。\\n\\nControlling for entropy 后 action-change-success correlation 从 0.08 降至 0.03（p=0.42，not significant）。这证明 plan_005 中观察到的微弱 correlation 完全由 entropy confound 解释：高 entropy → 更多 random action change + 更低 success。Action change 本身无 causal relationship with success。Reviewer concern 'action change = noise' 被证实。\"\n455\t  },\n456\t  {\n457\t    \"name\": \"Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes\",\n458\t    \"description\": \"Inject random action changes at same rate，对比 verification-triggered。\",\n459\t    \"results\": {\n460\t      \"success_rate_verification_triggered\": 0.22,\n461\t      \"success_rate_random_change\": 0.19,\n462\t      \"delta_pp\": 3.0,\n463\t      \"p_value\": 0.31,\n464\t      \"effect_size_cohens_d\": 0.12\n465\t    },\n466\t    \"tables\": [],\n467\t    \"figures\": [],\n468\t    \"analysis\": \"Verification 在 weak agent 上 ≈ random perturbation。这是 Claim 2 的 death blow——不仅 action-change 不是好 reward（plan_010），verification 本身在当前 agent 能力下就没有 causal value（它的 correction 不比 random good）。\\n\\nVerification-triggered changes 只比 random changes 好 3pp（not significant, p=0.31）。Effect size tiny (d=0.12)。原因：28% success 的 agent 做 verification 时，其 'correction' 几乎等价于 random re-sampling from policy——agent 没有真正的 'second opinion' 能力，verification output 和 original output 来自同一个 weak policy distribution。Causal evidence for verification value 不成立。\"\n469\t  },\n470\t  {\n471\t    \"name\": \"Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\",\n472\t    \"description\": \"比较不同 reward signals 训练 selective policy。\",\n473\t    \"results\": {\n474\t      \"action_change_success\": 0.219,\n475\t      \"action_change_verify_rate\": 0.88,\n476\t      \"random_trigger_success\": 0.234,\n477\t      \"random_trigger_verify_rate\": 0.52,\n478\t      \"confidence_reward_success\": 0.25,\n479\t      \"confidence_reward_verify_rate\": 0.65\n480\t    },\n481\t    \"tables\": [\n482\t      {\n483\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: Reward signal comparison\",\n484\t        \"columns\": [\n485\t          \"reward_type\",\n486\t          \"success\",\n487\t          \"verify_rate\",\n488\t          \"pareto_dominated\"\n489\t        ],\n490\t        \"rows\": [\n491\t          [\n492\t            \"action-change (ours)\",\n493\t            \"21.9%\",\n494\t            \"88%\",\n495\t            \"Yes (by all others)\"\n496\t          ],\n497\t          [\n498\t            \"random trigger\",\n499\t            \"23.4%\",\n500\t            \"52%\",\n501\t            \"No\"\n502\t          ],\n503\t          [\n504\t            \"confidence-based\",\n505\t            \"25.0%\",\n506\t            \"65%\",\n507\t            \"No\"\n508\t          ]\n509\t        ]\n510\t      }\n511\t    ],\n512\t    \"figures\": [],\n513\t    \"analysis\": \"Action-change reward 是 worst performer。Claim 2 ('action-change is effective intrinsic reward') 被彻底 falsified。Paper 失去了 selective verification 的 technical contribution。\\n\\n所有 reward variants 都 fail 达到 target，但 action-change 是最差的——它训出 near-always-verify 因为 reward signal 是 noise（plan_010 已证明）。Random trigger 反而学到 reasonable skip rate 因为 random reward 至少不 mislead（均匀分布）。Confidence 略好因为 confidence 与 success 有 weak correlation。讽刺：learned reward (action-change) 输给了 uninformed baselines。\"\n514\t  },\n515\t  {\n516\t    \"name\": \"ARES reproduction + comparison\",\n517\t    \"description\": \"Reproduce ARES SFT router, head-to-head 对比。\",\n518\t    \"results\": {\n519\t      \"ares_success\": 0.25,\n520\t      \"ares_verification_rate\": 0.55,\n521\t      \"ares_cost_reduction\": 0.38,\n522\t      \"biavr_success\": 0.219,\n523\t      \"biavr_verification_rate\": 0.88,\n524\t      \"biavr_cost_reduction\": 0.12,\n525\t      \"ares_dominates_biavr\": true\n526\t    },\n527\t    \"tables\": [],\n528\t    \"figures\": [],\n529\t    \"analysis\": \"SFT approach (ARES) 优于 RL approach (B-IAVR) 在这个 setting 下。原因：SFT 有 oracle supervision（从 data 直接学 when to verify），不受 reward noise 影响。RL 需要 good reward signal 但我们没有。Paper 的 'RL > SFT for selective verification' implicit claim 被反驳。\\n\\nARES 用 SFT 从 oracle decisions 学 router，不需要 RL reward signal quality。在 same base agent 上 ARES 能学到 55% verification rate 且保持 success（因为它直接学 'when did verification change outcome' from data），而 B-IAVR 依赖 noisy RL reward 学不到 meaningful policy。ARES 在 Pareto frontier 上 dominate B-IAVR。我们不仅没有 '≥10pp better cost reduction'，反而被 dominated。\"\n530\t  },\n531\t  {\n532\t    \"name\": \"ScienceWorld transfer\",\n533\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld。\",\n534\t    \"results\": {\n535\t      \"episode_level_success\": 0.15,\n536\t      \"step_independent_success\": 0.12,\n537\t      \"ratio\": 1.25,\n538\t      \"episode_level_std\": 0.06,\n539\t      \"step_independent_std\": 0.08,\n540\t      \"difference_significant\": false,\n541\t      \"p_value\": 0.38\n542\t    },\n543\t    \"tables\": [\n544\t      {\n545\t        \"name\": \"Table 8: ScienceWorld transfer\",\n546\t        \"columns\": [\n547\t          \"method\",\n548\t          \"success\",\n549\t          \"std\",\n550\t          \"avg_episode_length\"\n551\t        ],\n552\t        \"rows\": [\n553\t          [\n554\t            \"episode-level\",\n555\t            \"15.0%\",\n556\t            \"6pp\",\n557\t            \"12.3 steps\"\n558\t          ],\n559\t          [\n560\t            \"step-independent (h=5)\",\n561\t            \"12.0%\",\n562\t            \"8pp\",\n563\t            \"12.3 steps\"\n564\t          ]\n565\t        ]\n566\t      }\n567\t    ],\n568\t    \"figures\": [],\n569\t    \"analysis\": \"Episode-level advantage 不 generalize to shorter-horizon tasks。ScienceWorld 的短 episode 使 step-independent 的缺陷不 manifest。Reviewer concern #5 (single environment) 被证实——our finding is ALFWorld-specific (long horizon)，不是 general principle。\\n\\nWorst 档下 scienceworld_episode_vs_step_ratio 在 [0.8, 1.5]。Ratio=1.25 意味着 episode-level 只是 marginally better（15% vs 12%，差异 3pp not significant p=0.38）。ScienceWorld 有更短的 episodes（~10-15 steps vs ALFWorld 30-50），所以 step-independent 的 information loss 没那么严重——shorter episodes = fewer windows = less sign misattribution。这反驳了 'episode-level universally superior' claim，支持 'advantage depends on episode length' 的 nuanced view，但也意味着我们的 contribution 是 domain-specific 而非 general。\"\n570\t  },\n571\t  {\n572\t    \"name\": \"7B model scaling verification\",\n573\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-7B 上验证 episode-level vs step-independent。\",\n574\t    \"results\": {\n575\t      \"episode_level_7b_success\": 0.35,\n576\t      \"step_independent_7b_success\": 0.22,\n577\t      \"delta_pp\": 13,\n578\t      \"relative_improvement\": 1.59,\n579\t      \"step_independent_collapse\": false,\n580\t      \"step_independent_7b_h5_success\": 0.18\n581\t    },\n582\t    \"tables\": [\n583\t      {\n584\t        \"name\": \"Table 9: 7B scaling\",\n585\t        \"columns\": [\n586\t          \"method\",\n587\t          \"1.7B\",\n588\t          \"7B\",\n589\t          \"gap_reduction\"\n590\t        ],\n591\t        \"rows\": [\n592\t          [\n593\t            \"episode-level\",\n594\t            \"28.1%\",\n595\t            \"35%\",\n596\t            \"—\"\n597\t          ],\n598\t          [\n599\t            \"step-independent (h=5)\",\n600\t            \"0%\",\n601\t            \"22%\",\n602\t            \"Gap: 28pp→13pp\"\n603\t          ]\n604\t        ]\n605\t      }\n606\t    ],\n607\t    \"figures\": [],\n608\t    \"analysis\": \"Episode-level advantage diminishes with model scale。7B step-independent 不崩溃（22%），gap 缩小到 13pp。暗示 'catastrophic failure' 是 small model + long horizon 的特定 interaction，更大模型的 in-context learning 能部分补偿 credit assignment 缺陷。Paper 的 alarm ('step-independent catastrophically fails!') 变成了 'step-independent is suboptimal for small models on long tasks'——much weaker claim。\\n\\n7B 模型更强，step-independent 不完全崩溃（22% vs 1.7B 的 0%）。原因：更大模型有更好的 in-context learning，即使 h=5 窗口也能从有限 context 推断 partial strategy。Episode-level 仍优（35% vs 22%）但 gap 缩小（13pp vs 1.7B 的 28pp）。这进一步削弱 'catastrophic failure' narrative——在 stronger model 上 step-independent 只是 suboptimal 而非 catastrophic。Reviewer 会问 'at what model size does the gap disappear entirely?'\"\n609\t  },\n610\t  {\n611\t    \"name\": \"Per-task-type breakdown analysis\",\n612\t    \"description\": \"按 ALFWorld task type 分解 success。\",\n613\t    \"results\": {\n614\t      \"pick_success\": 0.35,\n615\t      \"clean_success\": 0.25,\n616\t      \"heat_success\": 0.3,\n617\t      \"cool_success\": 0.2,\n618\t      \"examine_success\": 0.15,\n619\t      \"pick_two_success\": 0.1,\n620\t      \"episode_length_correlation\": 0.45,\n621\t      \"longest_task_success\": 0.1,\n622\t      \"shortest_task_success\": 0.35\n623\t    },\n624\t    \"tables\": [\n625\t      {\n626\t        \"name\": \"Table 10: Per-task breakdown\",\n627\t        \"columns\": [\n628\t          \"task_type\",\n629\t          \"success\",\n630\t          \"avg_episode_length\",\n631\t          \"step_indep_success\"\n632\t        ],\n633\t        \"rows\": [\n634\t          [\n635\t            \"pick\",\n636\t            \"35%\",\n637\t            \"15\",\n638\t            \"8%\"\n639\t          ],\n640\t          [\n641\t            \"heat\",\n642\t            \"30%\",\n643\t            \"22\",\n644\t            \"3%\"\n645\t          ],\n646\t          [\n647\t            \"clean\",\n648\t            \"25%\",\n649\t            \"28\",\n650\t            \"0%\"\n651\t          ],\n652\t          [\n653\t            \"cool\",\n654\t            \"20%\",\n655\t            \"25\",\n656\t            \"2%\"\n657\t          ],\n658\t          [\n659\t            \"examine\",\n660\t            \"15%\",\n661\t            \"38\",\n662\t            \"0%\"\n663\t          ],\n664\t          [\n665\t            \"pick_two\",\n666\t            \"10%\",\n667\t            \"45\",\n668\t            \"0%\"\n669\t          ]\n670\t        ]\n671\t      }\n672\t    ],\n673\t    \"figures\": [],\n674\t    \"analysis\": \"Task length 是 contributing factor 但非唯一因素。Paper 可以 claim 'longer tasks benefit more' 但不能 claim 'length is the mechanism'。Adds nuance but not a strong independent contribution。\\n\\n较短 task（pick: ~15 steps）success 较高（35%），较长 task（pick_two: ~45 steps, examine: ~40 steps）success 最低（10-15%）。Episode length correlation=0.45 (moderate)。这 partially 支持 'longer tasks benefit more from episode-level'，但 correlation 不够 strong——其他 factors（task complexity, number of required objects）也 matter。Not a clean story。\"\n675\t  }\n676\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c2660b0-4796-4ae9-aeba-251df77b8a7c","uuid":"301d39c2-90cb-438c-9d61-90dfc2d3780f","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:55:58.611Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T133129/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Context window h-sweep ablation (3 seeds each)\",\n    \"description\": \"Sweep h={2, 5, 10, 20, full}, 15 steps, 3 seeds each. 测试 credit assignment cliff 是否 robust。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"h2_seed1_val_success_step15\": 0.0,\n      \"h2_seed2_val_success_step15\": 0.031,\n      \"h2_seed3_val_success_step15\": 0.0,\n      \"h5_seed1_val_success_step15\": 0.156,\n      \"h5_seed2_val_success_step15\": 0.0,\n      \"h5_seed3_val_success_step15\": 0.188,\n      \"h10_seed1_val_success_step15\": 0.094,\n      \"h10_seed2_val_success_step15\": 0.219,\n      \"h10_seed3_val_success_step15\": 0.125,\n      \"h20_seed1_val_success_step15\": 0.188,\n      \"h20_seed2_val_success_step15\": 0.25,\n      \"h20_seed3_val_success_step15\": 0.156,\n      \"full_seed1_val_success_step15\": 0.25,\n      \"full_seed2_val_success_step15\": 0.281,\n      \"full_seed3_val_success_step15\": 0.219,\n      \"collapse_rate_h2\": 0.67,\n      \"collapse_rate_h5\": 0.33,\n      \"collapse_rate_h10\": 0.0,\n      \"cliff_threshold_range\": \"3-8 (seed-dependent)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: h-sweep results (mean ± std across 3 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"h\",\n          \"val_success_mean\",\n          \"val_success_std\",\n          \"collapse_rate\",\n          \"convergence_step\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            \"1.0%\",\n            \"1.8%\",\n            \"67%\",\n            \"3-4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            \"11.5%\",\n            \"10.4%\",\n            \"33%\",\n            \"4-6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            10,\n            \"14.6%\",\n            \"6.3%\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"N/A\"\n          ],\n          [\n            20,\n            \"19.8%\",\n            \"4.8%\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"N/A\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"full\",\n            \"25.0%\",\n            \"3.1%\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"N/A\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cliff 不 robust。h=5 std=10.4pp 意味着 cliff 位置是 random variable 而非 structural property。无法 claim 'h<X catastrophically fails' 因为 X 取决于 seed。这削弱了 paper 的核心 figure 说服力——reviewer 会问 'with more seeds would the cliff disappear entirely?'\\n\\nWorst 档下 h-sweep cliff 不一致。h=2 多数 seed 崩溃但非全部（seed2 靠运气学到少量 pattern）。h=5 更关键：seed1/3 没有崩溃且学到 15-19%，只有 seed2 崩溃。这直接削弱 'catastrophic failure below threshold' narrative——cliff 位置是 stochastic 的，不是 deterministic 的。h=10/20/full 之间差异不大（均在 10-25% 区间），说明即使给了足够 context，episode-level 本身也有天花板。Monotonic degradation 假设不成立：h=5 的某些 seed 可以接近 h=full。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-seed replication (5 seeds total)\",\n    \"description\": \"4 additional seeds for exp029 episode-level config, report mean ± std。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_val_success_step15\": 0.281,\n      \"seed2_val_success_step15\": 0.188,\n      \"seed3_val_success_step15\": 0.313,\n      \"seed4_val_success_step15\": 0.156,\n      \"seed5_val_success_step15\": 0.25,\n      \"mean_val_success\": 0.238,\n      \"std_val_success\": 0.062,\n      \"max_val_success_any_seed\": 0.313,\n      \"min_val_success_any_seed\": 0.156,\n      \"seeds_above_30pct\": 1,\n      \"seeds_below_20pct\": 1,\n      \"convergence_step_range\": \"10-15 (all plateau)\",\n      \"step50_mean_val_success\": 0.26,\n      \"step50_std\": 0.071\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Multi-seed episode-level GRPO results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"seed\",\n          \"step5_val\",\n          \"step10_val\",\n          \"step15_val\",\n          \"step50_val\",\n          \"plateau_onset\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            \"25.0%\",\n            \"25.0%\",\n            \"28.1%\",\n            \"28.1%\",\n            \"step 10\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"18.8%\",\n            \"18.8%\",\n            \"18.8%\",\n            \"21.9%\",\n            \"step 5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            \"25.0%\",\n            \"31.3%\",\n            \"31.3%\",\n            \"31.3%\",\n            \"step 10\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"12.5%\",\n            \"15.6%\",\n            \"15.6%\",\n            \"15.6%\",\n            \"step 5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            \"18.8%\",\n            \"25.0%\",\n            \"25.0%\",\n            \"28.1%\",\n            \"step 10\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Mean 23.8% ± 6.2pp。95% CI = [11.3%, 36.3%]。这个 CI 与 step-independent h=10 mean（14.6%）有 overlap，削弱 episode-level 的统计 significance。更致命的是 plateau 现象——所有 seed 在 step 10-15 停滞，额外训练 35 步几乎无改善，说明 episode-level GRPO 本身有信息瓶颈（无 per-token credit）。\\n\\nWorst 档要求 multi_seed_std > 8pp。5 seeds 中 std=6.2pp（接近但略低于阈值），但如果看 step 50（训练更久），seed 4 可能进一步恶化（plateau 后缓慢下降到 12-15%），使得 late-stage std 达到 8-10pp。关键问题：seed 4 只有 15.6%，与 step-independent h=10 的 best seed（21.9%）重叠——episode-level 的 advantage over step-independent 在 per-seed 层面不 universal。reproducibility 不够 strong（CI 太宽），reviewer 会 flag 'your method might just be getting lucky on some seeds'。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GAE baseline comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"GAE(λ=0.95, γ=1.0) 和 GAE(λ=1.0, γ=1.0) vs episode-level GRPO, 15 steps × 3 seeds。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gae_095_mean_val_success_step15\": 0.438,\n      \"gae_095_std\": 0.047,\n      \"gae_100_mean_val_success_step15\": 0.375,\n      \"gae_100_std\": 0.055,\n      \"episode_grpo_mean_val_success_step15\": 0.238,\n      \"gae_095_vs_episode_delta_pp\": 20.0,\n      \"gae_100_vs_episode_delta_pp\": 13.7,\n      \"gae_095_action_is_valid\": 0.78,\n      \"gae_095_convergence_step\": 12,\n      \"gae_still_improving_at_step15\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: GAE vs Episode-level GRPO\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"val_success_mean\",\n          \"std\",\n          \"delta_vs_episode_grpo\",\n          \"action_is_valid\",\n          \"still_improving\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Episode GRPO\",\n            \"23.8%\",\n            \"6.2pp\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"55%\",\n            \"No (plateau)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GAE(λ=1.0,γ=1.0)\",\n            \"37.5%\",\n            \"5.5pp\",\n            \"+13.7pp\",\n            \"72%\",\n            \"Marginal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GAE(λ=0.95,γ=1.0)\",\n            \"43.8%\",\n            \"4.7pp\",\n            \"+20.0pp\",\n            \"78%\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GAE 大幅超越 episode-level GRPO 证明 per-token temporal difference credit 是关键。Episode-level 的 'advantage sign is correct' 不够——你还需要 magnitude differentiation across tokens。这反驳了 contrarian positioning：社区追求 finer credit 是对的。Episode-level 只是 '方向不错但信息太粗' 的 solution。Paper 的核心 contribution（'coarser suffices'）被实验数据否定。\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设：GAE >> episode-level GRPO（delta > 15pp）。GAE(0.95) 有 value function 做 per-token credit assignment，能区分 trajectory 中好/坏 action 并精确更新。Episode-level GRPO 所有 token 共享一个 advantage（相当于 REINFORCE），缺乏 temporal difference 信息。20pp gap 证明 per-token credit 是关键——episode-level 'just knowing the outcome' 不够，你需要知道 which tokens contributed。这直接反驳 paper 的 contrarian claim 'coarser is better'。GAE(1.0,1.0) 稍弱因为 high variance（相当于 Monte Carlo），但仍优于 GRPO 因为 critic 提供 baseline。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Episode-level + valid_action_bonus (plateau-breaker)\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level + valid_action_bonus=0.05, 测试能否打破 plateau 且不 game。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"val_success_step15\": 0.25,\n      \"val_action_is_valid_step15\": 0.72,\n      \"val_action_is_valid_step30\": 0.85,\n      \"success_plateau_broken\": false,\n      \"reward_gaming_detected\": false,\n      \"valid_bonus_vs_task_ratio\": \"4.2:10 (per episode)\",\n      \"action_is_valid_improvement\": \"+17pp vs vanilla\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"D056 insight 部分正确（episode-level 不 game dense reward），但 plateau 不是 action_is_valid 造成的。Base agent 学会了 'speak the right language' 但不知道 'say the right thing'。Plateau 本质是 episode-level credit 太粗——all valid actions 获得相同 reinforcement signal，模型无法区分哪个 valid action 更好。\\n\\nEpisode-level 下 dense reward gaming 不发生（与 exp013f 对比，D056 insight 正确）。action_is_valid 从 55% 提升到 72-85%，模型确实学到了更多合法 action format。但 success rate 仍 plateau 在 25%——更多 valid actions ≠ 更好的 task strategy。模型能输出合法格式但不知道 WHICH valid action 能推进 task。Valid action bonus 解决的是 syntax 问题而非 semantics 问题。Plateau 未突破因为瓶颈不在 action validity 而在 credit assignment granularity（GAE 结果已证明）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Credit assignment mechanism empirical verification\",\n    \"description\": \"Per-window advantage logging 验证 sign misattribution 机制。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sign_vs_outcome_correlation\": 0.72,\n      \"sign_vs_local_quality_correlation\": 0.28,\n      \"gamma_k_magnitude_decay_r2\": 0.45,\n      \"episode_level_advantage_variance\": 0.0,\n      \"success_episodes_all_positive\": 0.85,\n      \"failure_episodes_all_negative\": 0.78,\n      \"mixed_sign_episodes_pct\": 0.18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: Advantage sign analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"theoretical_prediction\",\n          \"observed\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"sign-outcome corr\",\n            \">0.95\",\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"Exists but not dominant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"sign-local_quality corr\",\n            \"<0.1\",\n            \"0.28\",\n            \"Non-trivial local signal present\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"γ^k decay R²\",\n            \">0.8\",\n            \"0.45\",\n            \"Weak fit\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mixed-sign episodes\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"18%\",\n            \"Theory violation\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"episode-level variance\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"0\",\n            \"Confirmed (trivially)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Sign misattribution 是 real phenomenon 但 paper 需要大幅 soften claims。不能写 'advantage sign is entirely determined by episode outcome'——实际只有 72% correlation。Mixed-sign episodes 的存在说明 GRPO group normalization 引入了组内 local ranking 信号（当 group 中有 partial success 时）。Reviewer 会 attack：'your mechanism is one factor among several, not THE explanation'。这把论文从 'mechanistic explanation paper' 降级为 'we observed a contributing factor'。\\n\\nWorst 档下 sign misattribution 存在但非 dominant。sign_vs_outcome_correlation=0.72 说明 advantage sign 确实偏向 episode outcome，但 0.72 远非 'near 1.0' 的理论预测。28% 的 local quality correlation 说明 advantage 中有 non-trivial 的 local signal（GRPO 的 group normalization 引入了组内相对排序信息）。18% 的 episodes 出现 mixed signs（部分 window positive 部分 negative in same episode），这不符合 'pure sign misattribution' 理论（理论预测应为 0%）。γ^k decay R²=0.45 说明 magnitude 确实随 position 衰减但 fit 不好（noise 大）。总结：mechanism 存在但不 clean，empirical evidence 是 'moderate support' 而非 'strong confirmation'。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Action-change statistics from always-on runs\",\n    \"description\": \"从 exp029 checkpoints 收集 verification 后 action change 统计。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"action_change_rate\": 0.35,\n      \"confirmatory_rate\": 0.65,\n      \"action_change_success_correlation\": 0.08,\n      \"action_change_rate_success_episodes\": 0.38,\n      \"action_change_rate_failure_episodes\": 0.34,\n      \"per_task_variance\": \"high (pick: 0.25, clean: 0.45, heat: 0.30)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Action-change reward 的前提假设（'change = informative verification'）在这个 agent 能力水平下不成立。28% success 的 agent 做 verification 更像是 random re-sampling 而非 informed decision revision。Selective verification 的整个 Phase B 建立在沙子上——你需要一个足够强的 agent（≥50% success?）才能让 verification 成为 meaningful signal 而非 noise。\\n\\nBase agent 只有 28% success rate，大部分 verification 是在失败 trajectory 中进行的。Action change rate 35%（不是 >60% confirmatory 的预期？ 其实是——65% confirmatory 符合假设）。但关键问题：action_change_success_correlation 极低（0.08），说明 action change 与 episode success 几乎无关。在成功 episodes 中 change rate=38%，失败中=34%——差异 negligible。这意味着 action-change 作为 reward signal 没有 information content：改变 action 并不 predictive of 成功。原因：base agent 太弱（28% success），它的 verification 大多是 random perturbation 而非 informed correction。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Selective verification implementation\",\n    \"description\": \"实现 binary verify/skip decision。Code-only。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"implementation_complete\": true,\n      \"code_lines_added\": 280,\n      \"integration_test_pass\": true,\n      \"gpu_hours\": 0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Implementation 本身 trivial。问题不在代码而在 downstream training signal quality。\\n\\n纯代码实现，无 ML 依赖。能完成但实际 training（plan_007）会 fail 因为 base agent 太弱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"B-IAVR selective verification training\",\n    \"description\": \"从 exp029 best checkpoint 训练 selective verification policy。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"verification_rate\": 0.88,\n      \"success_rate\": 0.219,\n      \"success_delta_vs_always_on_pp\": -6.2,\n      \"cost_reduction\": 0.12,\n      \"training_converged\": false,\n      \"policy_behavior\": \"near-always-verify (degenerate)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: B-IAVR training results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"target\",\n          \"achieved\",\n          \"gap\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"verification_rate_reduction\",\n            \"≥40%\",\n            \"12%\",\n            \"-28pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"success_delta_vs_always_on\",\n            \"<5pp\",\n            \"-6.2pp\",\n            \"Fail\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cost_reduction_pct\",\n            \"≥40%\",\n            \"12%\",\n            \"-28pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"policy_entropy_final\",\n            \">0.3\",\n            \"0.08\",\n            \"Collapsed to always-verify\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Selective verification 在 base agent success < 30% 时完全不可行。Policy 无法学到 meaningful skip pattern 因为：(1) reward signal (action-change) 是 noise，(2) skipping has guaranteed downside with no upside at this performance level。整个 Phase B contribution 不成立。\\n\\nBase agent 只有 28% success。Selective policy 面临两个问题：(1) action-change reward 无 information content（plan_005 证明 change 与 success 无关），所以 reward signal is noise；(2) skip verification 有 immediate cost（performance drop），而 base agent 已经很弱，任何 skip 都大幅降低本就脆弱的 success rate。Policy 学到 degenerate solution：几乎 always verify（88% rate），偶尔 skip 是 random noise 而非 learned strategy。12% cost reduction 远未达到 40% target。Success 还 drop 了 6pp 因为那 12% skip 确实 hurt。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Selective verification full comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold 对比。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"always_on_success\": 0.281,\n      \"biavr_success\": 0.219,\n      \"biavr_verification_rate\": 0.88,\n      \"no_verify_success\": 0.188,\n      \"random_p05_success\": 0.234,\n      \"random_p05_verification_rate\": 0.5,\n      \"confidence_threshold_success\": 0.25,\n      \"confidence_threshold_verification_rate\": 0.62\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: Verification strategy comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"success\",\n          \"verify_rate\",\n          \"cost_tokens\",\n          \"success_per_token\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"always-on\",\n            \"28.1%\",\n            \"100%\",\n            \"1.00x\",\n            \"0.281\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B-IAVR (ours)\",\n            \"21.9%\",\n            \"88%\",\n            \"0.92x\",\n            \"0.238\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random-p=0.5\",\n            \"23.4%\",\n            \"50%\",\n            \"0.67x\",\n            \"0.349\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"confidence\",\n            \"25.0%\",\n            \"62%\",\n            \"0.74x\",\n            \"0.338\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"no-verify\",\n            \"18.8%\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"0.45x\",\n            \"0.418\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Paper Claim 3 完全 fail。B-IAVR 被 naive baselines dominate。讽刺的是 no-verify 的 efficiency 最高（per-token success ratio），说明在 28% success 水平下，verification 本身就是 pure overhead——agent 改变 action 不提升 success。\\n\\nB-IAVR 不 dominate Pareto frontier。Random-p=0.5 在 success/cost tradeoff 上 comparable to B-IAVR（random: 23.4% success at 50% cost vs B-IAVR: 21.9% at 88% cost）——random 更 cost-efficient。Confidence threshold 也优于 B-IAVR。这证明 learned policy 不优于 naive baselines，因为 base agent 太弱导致所有 verification 策略 degenerate。No-verify 只 drop 9pp（远低于预期的 ≥10pp），说明 verification 本身 value 也有限。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"No-verify ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level GRPO without self-verification。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"success_rate\": 0.188,\n      \"action_is_valid\": 0.52,\n      \"delta_vs_always_on\": -9.3\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Verification value 存在但 modest（9pp）。不足以支撑 'selective verification 是重要 research problem' 的 motivation——reviewer 会说 'if verification only adds 9pp, why not just skip it entirely and save tokens?'\\n\\nNo-verify 只 drop ~9pp（28.1% → 18.8%），低于预期的 ≥10pp。原因：在 28% success level，verification 的 marginal value 有限——agent 的 success 主要来自偶然走对 path，verification 只是小幅增加 correction 机会但不 fundamentally 改变 strategy。如果 base agent 更强（如 GAE 的 44%），verification drop 可能更大，但我们无法测试因为 episode-level 训练不出更强的 agent。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Stratify by policy entropy，测试 action-change-success correlation 是否 holds。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"partial_correlation_after_entropy_control\": 0.03,\n      \"p_value\": 0.42,\n      \"low_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.05,\n      \"high_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.11,\n      \"entropy_success_correlation\": -0.15\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Action-change 作为 verification informativeness proxy 的理论基础被否定。Change 只是 high entropy 的 side effect，不是 'verification found better action'。Claim 2 的 reward design 无 empirical grounding。\\n\\nControlling for entropy 后 action-change-success correlation 从 0.08 降至 0.03（p=0.42，not significant）。这证明 plan_005 中观察到的微弱 correlation 完全由 entropy confound 解释：高 entropy → 更多 random action change + 更低 success。Action change 本身无 causal relationship with success。Reviewer concern 'action change = noise' 被证实。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes\",\n    \"description\": \"Inject random action changes at same rate，对比 verification-triggered。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"success_rate_verification_triggered\": 0.22,\n      \"success_rate_random_change\": 0.19,\n      \"delta_pp\": 3.0,\n      \"p_value\": 0.31,\n      \"effect_size_cohens_d\": 0.12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Verification 在 weak agent 上 ≈ random perturbation。这是 Claim 2 的 death blow——不仅 action-change 不是好 reward（plan_010），verification 本身在当前 agent 能力下就没有 causal value（它的 correction 不比 random good）。\\n\\nVerification-triggered changes 只比 random changes 好 3pp（not significant, p=0.31）。Effect size tiny (d=0.12)。原因：28% success 的 agent 做 verification 时，其 'correction' 几乎等价于 random re-sampling from policy——agent 没有真正的 'second opinion' 能力，verification output 和 original output 来自同一个 weak policy distribution。Causal evidence for verification value 不成立。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\",\n    \"description\": \"比较不同 reward signals 训练 selective policy。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"action_change_success\": 0.219,\n      \"action_change_verify_rate\": 0.88,\n      \"random_trigger_success\": 0.234,\n      \"random_trigger_verify_rate\": 0.52,\n      \"confidence_reward_success\": 0.25,\n      \"confidence_reward_verify_rate\": 0.65\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: Reward signal comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"reward_type\",\n          \"success\",\n          \"verify_rate\",\n          \"pareto_dominated\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"action-change (ours)\",\n            \"21.9%\",\n            \"88%\",\n            \"Yes (by all others)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random trigger\",\n            \"23.4%\",\n            \"52%\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"confidence-based\",\n            \"25.0%\",\n            \"65%\",\n            \"No\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Action-change reward 是 worst performer。Claim 2 ('action-change is effective intrinsic reward') 被彻底 falsified。Paper 失去了 selective verification 的 technical contribution。\\n\\n所有 reward variants 都 fail 达到 target，但 action-change 是最差的——它训出 near-always-verify 因为 reward signal 是 noise（plan_010 已证明）。Random trigger 反而学到 reasonable skip rate 因为 random reward 至少不 mislead（均匀分布）。Confidence 略好因为 confidence 与 success 有 weak correlation。讽刺：learned reward (action-change) 输给了 uninformed baselines。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ARES reproduction + comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Reproduce ARES SFT router, head-to-head 对比。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ares_success\": 0.25,\n      \"ares_verification_rate\": 0.55,\n      \"ares_cost_reduction\": 0.38,\n      \"biavr_success\": 0.219,\n      \"biavr_verification_rate\": 0.88,\n      \"biavr_cost_reduction\": 0.12,\n      \"ares_dominates_biavr\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SFT approach (ARES) 优于 RL approach (B-IAVR) 在这个 setting 下。原因：SFT 有 oracle supervision（从 data 直接学 when to verify），不受 reward noise 影响。RL 需要 good reward signal 但我们没有。Paper 的 'RL > SFT for selective verification' implicit claim 被反驳。\\n\\nARES 用 SFT 从 oracle decisions 学 router，不需要 RL reward signal quality。在 same base agent 上 ARES 能学到 55% verification rate 且保持 success（因为它直接学 'when did verification change outcome' from data），而 B-IAVR 依赖 noisy RL reward 学不到 meaningful policy。ARES 在 Pareto frontier 上 dominate B-IAVR。我们不仅没有 '≥10pp better cost reduction'，反而被 dominated。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ScienceWorld transfer\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"episode_level_success\": 0.15,\n      \"step_independent_success\": 0.12,\n      \"ratio\": 1.25,\n      \"episode_level_std\": 0.06,\n      \"step_independent_std\": 0.08,\n      \"difference_significant\": false,\n      \"p_value\": 0.38\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 8: ScienceWorld transfer\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"success\",\n          \"std\",\n          \"avg_episode_length\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"episode-level\",\n            \"15.0%\",\n            \"6pp\",\n            \"12.3 steps\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"step-independent (h=5)\",\n            \"12.0%\",\n            \"8pp\",\n            \"12.3 steps\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Episode-level advantage 不 generalize to shorter-horizon tasks。ScienceWorld 的短 episode 使 step-independent 的缺陷不 manifest。Reviewer concern #5 (single environment) 被证实——our finding is ALFWorld-specific (long horizon)，不是 general principle。\\n\\nWorst 档下 scienceworld_episode_vs_step_ratio 在 [0.8, 1.5]。Ratio=1.25 意味着 episode-level 只是 marginally better（15% vs 12%，差异 3pp not significant p=0.38）。ScienceWorld 有更短的 episodes（~10-15 steps vs ALFWorld 30-50），所以 step-independent 的 information loss 没那么严重——shorter episodes = fewer windows = less sign misattribution。这反驳了 'episode-level universally superior' claim，支持 'advantage depends on episode length' 的 nuanced view，但也意味着我们的 contribution 是 domain-specific 而非 general。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"7B model scaling verification\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-7B 上验证 episode-level vs step-independent。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"episode_level_7b_success\": 0.35,\n      \"step_independent_7b_success\": 0.22,\n      \"delta_pp\": 13,\n      \"relative_improvement\": 1.59,\n      \"step_independent_collapse\": false,\n      \"step_independent_7b_h5_success\": 0.18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 9: 7B scaling\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"1.7B\",\n          \"7B\",\n          \"gap_reduction\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"episode-level\",\n            \"28.1%\",\n            \"35%\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"step-independent (h=5)\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"22%\",\n            \"Gap: 28pp→13pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Episode-level advantage diminishes with model scale。7B step-independent 不崩溃（22%），gap 缩小到 13pp。暗示 'catastrophic failure' 是 small model + long horizon 的特定 interaction，更大模型的 in-context learning 能部分补偿 credit assignment 缺陷。Paper 的 alarm ('step-independent catastrophically fails!') 变成了 'step-independent is suboptimal for small models on long tasks'——much weaker claim。\\n\\n7B 模型更强，step-independent 不完全崩溃（22% vs 1.7B 的 0%）。原因：更大模型有更好的 in-context learning，即使 h=5 窗口也能从有限 context 推断 partial strategy。Episode-level 仍优（35% vs 22%）但 gap 缩小（13pp vs 1.7B 的 28pp）。这进一步削弱 'catastrophic failure' narrative——在 stronger model 上 step-independent 只是 suboptimal 而非 catastrophic。Reviewer 会问 'at what model size does the gap disappear entirely?'\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-task-type breakdown analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"按 ALFWorld task type 分解 success。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"pick_success\": 0.35,\n      \"clean_success\": 0.25,\n      \"heat_success\": 0.3,\n      \"cool_success\": 0.2,\n      \"examine_success\": 0.15,\n      \"pick_two_success\": 0.1,\n      \"episode_length_correlation\": 0.45,\n      \"longest_task_success\": 0.1,\n      \"shortest_task_success\": 0.35\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 10: Per-task breakdown\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"task_type\",\n          \"success\",\n          \"avg_episode_length\",\n          \"step_indep_success\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"pick\",\n            \"35%\",\n            \"15\",\n            \"8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"heat\",\n            \"30%\",\n            \"22\",\n            \"3%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"clean\",\n            \"25%\",\n            \"28\",\n            \"0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cool\",\n            \"20%\",\n            \"25\",\n            \"2%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"examine\",\n            \"15%\",\n            \"38\",\n            \"0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"pick_two\",\n            \"10%\",\n            \"45\",\n            \"0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Task length 是 contributing factor 但非唯一因素。Paper 可以 claim 'longer tasks benefit more' 但不能 claim 'length is the mechanism'。Adds nuance but not a strong independent contribution。\\n\\n较短 task（pick: ~15 steps）success 较高（35%），较长 task（pick_two: ~45 steps, examine: ~40 steps）success 最低（10-15%）。Episode length correlation=0.45 (moderate)。这 partially 支持 'longer tasks benefit more from episode-level'，但 correlation 不够 strong——其他 factors（task complexity, number of required objects）也 matter。Not a clean story。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":676,"startLine":1,"totalLines":676}}}
